{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on question 4a13a195 and on the checker's note ede60bc1: the\nreview goes ahead on the set that stands. No refiling now.\n\nFacts. The stale mark is a projection over Rests-On. Supersede\nae9d8483 retired review request d39e5ee5, and the mark reached every\nact that rests on it. No code and no evidence changed. On 25 October\nthe Site recovery head landed with a stale approval chain: `gs merge`\nlanded the head and wrote the stale bases into the receipt. The\nrefusal \"describes a superseded world\" applies only when the retired\nancestor is an artifact. Here the retired ancestor is a request.\n\n1. Checker: review head de980a3d and file the verdict against review\n   request 3e0f9278 and its 25 artifacts, primary c71ecb88. Run\n   `gs review --prepare` first. A stale mark on the set is no finding.\n2. Builder: after an approval, ratify and run `gs merge-plan`. The\n   plan is the test. If it allows the landing, land. The receipt then\n   carries the stale bases, and that record is enough.\n3. Only if `gs review` or `gs merge-plan` refuses because of the stale\n   mark, refresh in this way. Do not publish a path twice at de980a3d.\n   Add one empty commit on de980a3d. Publish the 25 paths at the new\n   head on promise 5a78 alone. Name 8105f25b, 15d3b0bd and 337840eb in\n   the note's text as history, not as bases. File the review request\n   with --replace. The sealed focus, the control and the exact-head CI\n   carry to the new head by tree equality: `git rev-parse \u003cnew\u003e^{tree}`\n   prints 1c2eea2a. No test, control, build or CI run repeats, and the\n   checker's content review carries too.\n4. Ruling 15d3b0bd stands as written. This act restates it on the live\n   request a30f1b67: the Git-parent repair needs the 37-case focus, one\n   mutant control and exact-head CI, and no second whole gate. All\n   three are done.\n\nFor later heads: when a new review request replaces a reported one,\nrest the new artifacts on the promise alone. Name an old verdict in\nthe text.\n\nMain stays at ab802614 until (b) lands. The sprint report waits.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}